==================================================================1500 1451   22
  MF/MT combinations used to define ALL electron interaction data 1500 1451   23
  are newly defined MF/MT numbers for ENDF/B-VI that did not exist1500 1451   24
  in earlier versions of ENDF/B.                                  1500 1451   25
==================================================================1500 1451   26
  Definition of Data                                              1500 1451   27
==================================================================1500 1451   28
  Atomic Relaxation Data for Electrons and Photons                1500 1451   29
==================================================================1500 1451   30
1) An atom can be ionized by a photon or an electron interaction. 1500 1451   31
2) The atomic relaxation data included here describes how a       1500 1451   32
   singly ionized atom returns to neutrality, by emitting photons 1500 1451   33
   (x-rays) and/or electrons (Auger, Coster-Kronig).              1500 1451   34
3) Data is given to define the transition probabilities between   1500 1451   35
   subshells for radiative (x-ray emission) and non-radiative     1500 1451   36
   (Auger, Coster-Kronig) transitions.                            1500 1451   37
4) The complete spectrum of emitted photons and electrons can be  1500 1451   38
   calculated using the data included here, e.g., see ref. 2,     1500 1451   39
   below, for am example of a computer code that analytically     1500 1451   40
   calculates these spectra.                                      1500 1451   41
==================================================================1500 1451   42
  References                                                      1500 1451   43
==================================================================1500 1451   44
1) S.T. Perkins, D.E. Cullen, etal., "Tables and Graphs of Atomic 1500 1451   45
   Subshell and Relaxation Data Derived from the LLNL Evaluated   1500 1451   46
   Atomic Data Library (EADL), Z = 1 - 100", UCRL-50400, Vol. 30, 1500 1451   47
   Lawrence Livermore National Laboratory (1991).                 1500 1451   48
2) D.E. Cullen "Program RELAX: A Code Designed to Calculate X-Ray 1500 1451   49
   and Electron Emission Spectra as Singly Charged Atoms Relax    1500 1451   50
   Back to Neutrality", UCRL-ID-110438, Lawrence Livermore        1500 1451   51
   National Laboratory (1992).                                    1500 1451   52
                                                                  1500 1451   53
  These are the primary references to the contents of this library1500 1451   54
  and they contain a complete list of references to the sources   1500 1451   55
  of data used in this library, methods of evaluation, accuracy   1500 1451   56
  of the data, etc.                                               1500 1451   57
==================================================================1500 1451   58
  History                                                         1500 1451   59
==================================================================1500 1451   60
 (1) November, 1991 - Initial release in the ENDL format.         1500 1451   61
 (2) October,  2001 - Initial release in the ENDF-6 format.       1500 1451   62
